    "result_text": "The build passes with all 29 tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule in the owner-creation endpoint (`POST /api/owners`), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`): before saving a new owner, count the existing owners whose city matches the incoming owner's city, and reject with **409 Conflict** when that count is already 50 or more:\n\n```java\nString cityKey = householdKey(owner.getCity());\nlong cityCount = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .filter(existing -> existing.getCity() != null\n        && cityKey.equals(householdKey(existing.getCity())))\n    .count();\nif (cityCount >= 50) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\nThe comparison reuses the existing `householdKey` normalization (trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase), matching how the surrounding code (e.g. `nextCustomerCode`) already counts owners per city \u2014 so the cap is applied case-insensitively and consistently. The 51st owner in a city (created when 50 already exist) is rejected.\n\nAll existing and acceptance tests pass: `Tests run: 29, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
